#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:2
msgid "Coroutines"
msgstr "Coroutine"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:4
msgid ""
"A *coroutine* is a function that can pause partway through and later resume "
"from where it left off, with all its local variables intact. It mirrors the "
"generator pattern -- a function body that can be suspended and resumed -- "
"with one change in who drives each resume."
msgstr ""
"Sebuah *coroutine* adalah fungsi yang dapat berhenti di tengah eksekusi dan "
"dilanjutkan kembali dari titik yang sama, dengan semua variabel lokalnya "
"tetap utuh. Ini mencerminkan pola generator -- sebuah badan fungsi yang "
"dapat ditangguhkan dan dilanjutkan -- dengan satu perbedaan: siapa yang "
"mengendalikan setiap pelanjutan."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:10
msgid ""
"Python's syntax for writing a coroutine is the ``async`` / ``await`` keyword"
" pair. ``async`` marks the function as a coroutine; ``await`` marks the "
"points inside it where pausing is allowed."
msgstr ""
"Sintaks Python untuk menulis coroutine adalah pasangan kata kunci ``async`` "
"/ ``await``\\ . ``async`` menandai fungsi sebagai coroutine; ``await`` "
"menandai titik-titik di dalamnya di mana penghentian sementara diizinkan."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:16
msgid "Defining a coroutine"
msgstr "Mendefinisikan coroutine"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:18
msgid ""
"A function defined with ``async def`` is a *coroutine function*. Calling it "
"does not run the body; it returns a *coroutine object* that has not started "
"yet:"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi yang didefinisikan dengan ``async def`` adalah *fungsi coroutine*\\ ."
" Memanggilnya tidak menjalankan badan fungsinya; melainkan mengembalikan "
"*objek coroutine* yang belum dimulai:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:29
msgid ""
"The coroutine object is paused at the very beginning of the function. "
"Something has to *drive* it to make the body run -- that something is an "
"event loop, a runtime component. MicroPython ships one in the :mod:`asyncio`"
" module. For now, treat the coroutine as \"ready to run, waiting for a "
"driver\"."
msgstr ""
"Objek coroutine ditangguhkan di awal fungsi. Sesuatu harus *mengendalikan* "
"coroutine agar badannya berjalan -- sesuatu itu adalah event loop, sebuah "
"komponen runtime. MicroPython menyertakannya dalam modul :mod:`asyncio`\\ . "
"Untuk saat ini, anggap coroutine sebagai \"siap dijalankan, menunggu "
"pengendali\"."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:36
msgid "Pausing inside a coroutine"
msgstr "Menghentikan sementara di dalam coroutine"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:38
msgid ""
"Inside a coroutine, an ``await`` expression suspends execution until the "
"awaited value is ready:"
msgstr ""
"Di dalam coroutine, ekspresi ``await`` menangguhkan eksekusi hingga nilai "
"yang ditunggu siap:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:47
msgid ""
"When the body reaches ``await read_sensor()``, the coroutine hands control "
"back to whatever is running it. When ``read_sensor()`` finishes, the driver "
"resumes the coroutine on the next line, with the result bound to ``data``."
msgstr ""
"Ketika badan fungsi mencapai ``await read_sensor()``\\ , coroutine "
"menyerahkan kendali kembali ke apapun yang menjalankannya. Ketika "
"``read_sensor()`` selesai, pengendali melanjutkan coroutine di baris "
"berikutnya, dengan hasilnya terikat ke ``data``\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:52
msgid ""
"``await`` is only valid inside a coroutine. Using it in a regular function "
"is a syntax error."
msgstr ""
"``await`` hanya berlaku di dalam coroutine. Menggunakannya dalam fungsi "
"biasa adalah kesalahan sintaks."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:56
msgid "Relationship to generators"
msgstr "Hubungan dengan generator"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:58
msgid ""
"Coroutines and generators share the same underlying mechanic. The split is "
"who pulls each resume:"
msgstr ""
"Coroutine dan generator berbagi mekanisme dasar yang sama. Perbedaannya "
"adalah siapa yang menarik setiap pelanjutan:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:61
msgid ""
"A generator yields *values*; the consumer pulls the next one with "
":func:`next` or by iterating."
msgstr ""
"Generator menghasilkan *nilai*\\ ; konsumen menarik nilai berikutnya dengan "
":func:`next` atau dengan melakukan iterasi."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:63
msgid ""
"A coroutine yields *control*; an event loop schedules the resume when the "
"awaited operation is ready."
msgstr ""
"Coroutine menghasilkan *kendali*\\ ; event loop menjadwalkan pelanjutan "
"ketika operasi yang ditunggu siap."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:66
msgid ""
"If the generator-yield handshake makes sense, the coroutine handshake is the"
" same idea -- just driven by an event loop instead of a ``for`` loop."
msgstr ""
"Jika jabat tangan generator-yield sudah dipahami, jabat tangan coroutine "
"adalah ide yang sama -- hanya dikendalikan oleh event loop, bukan loop "
"``for``\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:70
msgid ""
"An *event loop* is a small dispatcher that keeps a list of coroutines "
"waiting on something (a timer, a network event, another coroutine "
"finishing). Each iteration it picks a coroutine whose wait has been "
"satisfied, resumes it until the next ``await``, then records what that "
"coroutine is now waiting for and moves on to another ready one. The result "
"is many tasks making progress concurrently on a single thread -- each "
"coroutine voluntarily yields control at its ``await`` points, and the loop "
"fills those moments with whatever other coroutines are ready to make "
"progress."
msgstr ""
"Sebuah *event loop* adalah dispatcher kecil yang menyimpan daftar coroutine "
"yang menunggu sesuatu (timer, event jaringan, coroutine lain yang selesai). "
"Setiap iterasi, ia memilih coroutine yang penantiannya telah terpenuhi, "
"melanjutkannya hingga ``await`` berikutnya, lalu mencatat apa yang coroutine"
" itu tunggu sekarang dan beralih ke coroutine lain yang siap. Hasilnya "
"adalah banyak task yang membuat kemajuan secara bersamaan dalam satu thread "
"-- setiap coroutine secara sukarela menyerahkan kendali di titik-titik "
"``await``\\ -nya, dan loop mengisi momen-momen itu dengan coroutine lain "
"yang siap membuat kemajuan."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:81
msgid ""
"Under the hood, ``await`` and ``yield`` use the same Python runtime feature "
"for suspending and resuming a function. The keywords differ because the "
"convention around them does: ``yield`` hands a value back to a consumer "
"pulling with :func:`next`; ``await`` hands control to an event loop that "
"schedules the resume when the awaited operation is ready. ``async`` / "
"``await`` is essentially newer syntax for the coroutine pattern -- older "
"libraries built coroutines on top of the generator machinery directly, using"
" ``yield from`` (introduced on :doc:`iterators-and-generators`) to delegate "
"suspension between coroutines."
msgstr ""
"Di balik layar, ``await`` dan ``yield`` menggunakan fitur runtime Python "
"yang sama untuk menangguhkan dan melanjutkan fungsi. Kata kunci berbeda "
"karena konvensi di sekitarnya berbeda: ``yield`` menyerahkan nilai kembali "
"ke konsumen yang menarik dengan :func:`next`\\ ; ``await`` menyerahkan "
"kendali ke event loop yang menjadwalkan pelanjutan ketika operasi yang "
"ditunggu siap. ``async`` / ``await`` pada dasarnya adalah sintaks yang lebih"
" baru untuk pola coroutine -- pustaka lama membangun coroutine di atas "
"mekanisme generator secara langsung, menggunakan ``yield from`` "
"(diperkenalkan di :doc:`iterators-and-generators`\\ ) untuk mendelegasikan "
"penangguhan antar coroutine."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:94
msgid "Coroutines need a driver"
msgstr "Coroutine membutuhkan pengendali"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/iteration/coroutines.rst:96
msgid ""
"A coroutine is inert without a runtime to drive it. Defining one is fine; "
"running one needs an event loop. MicroPython's :mod:`asyncio` module "
"provides that event loop. The :doc:`Asyncio "
"</openmvcam/tutorial/asyncio/index>` section covers how to start the loop, "
"schedule coroutines on it, share state between them with locks and events, "
"handle cancellation and timeouts, and shape a real application around the "
"``async`` / ``await`` keywords introduced here."
msgstr ""
"Sebuah coroutine tidak aktif tanpa runtime untuk mengendalikannya. "
"Mendefinisikannya tidak masalah; menjalankannya membutuhkan event loop. "
"Modul :mod:`asyncio` MicroPython menyediakan event loop tersebut. Bagian "
":doc:`Asyncio </openmvcam/tutorial/asyncio/index>` membahas cara memulai "
"loop, menjadwalkan coroutine di dalamnya, berbagi state antar coroutine "
"dengan lock dan event, menangani pembatalan dan timeout, serta menyusun "
"aplikasi nyata berdasarkan kata kunci ``async`` / ``await`` yang "
"diperkenalkan di sini."
